{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact head 73d4056e43535d988795ab8c9418e5c8d0d1acb6 (tree 7aff63d531a73c3030a752bcc15e51f43667b331), BO1-W1 step 1 on published c02f76a0. The source change and its evidence are right. Four sentences in docs/security still describe the Commons configuration that this head removes, and they contradict it. The fix is a documents-only commit.\n\n## What is right\n- **Artifacts.** The three filed artifacts equal the three changed paths (`git diff --no-renames --name-only c02f76a0 73d4056e`): `apps/room/wrangler.commons.jsonc` (87462d71), the structure note (d37e597c) and `packages/cli/test/demo-config.test.ts` (3a6892ba). None is missing, extra or twice.\n- **Config.** The source diff to the Worker file has two edits: the comment now says \"two unplanned register fields\", and the `DEMO_START_CONFIG` entry is gone. `REGISTER_SCOPE` and `ARTIFACTS_CONFIG.registerScope` stay `unplanned`. The namespace, host, bindings, `PLATFORM_CREATION_PINS` cohort, `SCOPE_INDEX_MODE` (`enforce`), the empty `APPLICATION_SCREEN_HOSTS` and `APPLICATION_TRUST`, and the creation limits are untouched. Removing the setting removes the Page Start link, which the plan note says is the malformed offer (`fetch.ts` shows the link when the setting is present, and `unplanned` fails the Demo parser).\n- **Test.** `commonsRegisterPair` accepts the pair `unplanned`/`unplanned` or two equal valid scope IDs, and rejects missing, malformed and unequal values. The test takes a valid ID from the demo file and a different one from the grow file, and it asserts the Commons vars lack `DEMO_START_CONFIG`. It retains every other assertion of the old test and changes none of the namespace, binding or cohort checks. Its pin grammar will pass the timed commit that sets both values to one ID.\n- **Gate.** `gate.txt` (SHA-256 `e8185014…`) names head 8a9bcfc6, tree b03f0993, changed files 0, ends \"gate passed\", and `gate.exit` is 0 (1,283.25 s). The terminal evidence for Counting, Plain and Native is complete, and crossings are zero lost, two stale, zero unowned. The review head differs from 8a9bcfc6 only in the evidence note (`git diff --name-only 8a9bcfc6 73d4056e`). All six SHA-256 values in the note match the retained files.\n- **Scale tier.** The selector omitted scale (`outside-scale-paths`), as for E3. The GS-2 audit covers it.\n- **Checks.** The merge into origin/main is clean with tree 7aff63d5. `check-commit-messages` flags none of 2 commits, `check-notes` reports 0 warnings, and `git diff --check` is clean. The added lines carry no other project's name and no `/Users/` path outside the retained evidence directory.\n\n## Wake rate\nConfiguration and a test only. No alarm, retry or reschedule is added, so the wake floor and requests per room per hour are unchanged. The Worker is still not deployed. The plan note's idle baseline (at most 25 requests in 15 minutes before Hugh's block) governs its first hour.\n\n## Architecture\nThe separate Worker keeps one closed state. Both register values stay `unplanned` until the timed commit changes both to one ID, and the test now states that rule.\n\n## Security\nRemoving the Start setting removes the Page offer for a register that does not exist. No token, header, custody or admission path changes, and no setting is added. Creation stays closed while the pair is `unplanned`.\n\n## Simplification\nNothing to remove.\n\n## The defect\nThe head removes `DEMO_START_CONFIG` from the Commons file and says two register fields remain, but four sentences under docs/security say the opposite. The settings inventory test passes because it checks undocumented settings read, not stale Worker names.\n1. `docs/security/settings.md`, the `DEMO_START_CONFIG` row (line 191) lists `dap-commons` among the Workers that carry the setting. Remove `dap-commons` from that list.\n2. `docs/security/settings.md` (lines 46 to 51) says the Commons file holds `unplanned` \"in all three register positions\" and that \"Its Start configuration is retained metadata\". It now holds two positions and has no Start configuration.\n3. `docs/security/entry-points.md` (line 453) says \"Its three register fields hold `unplanned`\". It has two.\n4. `docs/security/trust-boundaries.md` (line 286) says \"The checked-in `DEMO_START_CONFIG` is not a Commons provisioning interface\" and that the Demo parser does not recognize Register 23. The Commons file has no such setting now. Say that the Commons configuration carries no `DEMO_START_CONFIG`, so its Page offers no Start link, and keep the sentence on the two operational register fields.\n\n## Fix\nMake one documents-only commit on 73d4056e that corrects those four places. Do not rerun the gate. docs/evidence-filing.md covers a document-only successor, and the source and tests stay those of 8a9bcfc6. File the three source artifacts as they are, and add the three docs paths as artifacts. I will check the four places against `git grep -n \"DEMO_START_CONFIG\\|three register\" -- docs` and the unchanged source.\n\n## Non-blocking\nThe plan's timed commit changes `REGISTER_SCOPE` and `ARTIFACTS_CONFIG.registerScope`. The new test already allows that pair, and the security settings owner reads the same file. Run `demo-config.test.ts`, `security-settings.test.mjs` and `npm run pins` on that commit, as ruling e53e0500 says.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:87462d7189d58f99982dd5bbf0445f2aa5158440","binding":"assigned","head":"73d4056e43535d988795ab8c9418e5c8d0d1acb6","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8a394752f21accf1bf8509ea1ef8179e1d2d73ba\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b8d7bd6cc04987a5eaac496925c70f22abb2f36f\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8a394752f21accf1bf8509ea1ef8179e1d2d73ba","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}